        "x1": 0.7325822596692184,
        "y1": 0.5210077763199634
      },
      "text": "Al2 h30 ≈ 1,",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.12910898514124347,
        "y0": 0.23919357961900806,
        "x1": 0.7782301181436813,
        "y1": 0.2884300749861818
      },
      "text": "Later, Panthee [4] improved this result by showing that the solution map is not continuous from Hs(R) to D′(R) for any ﬁxed t > 0 small enough.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7668903155665904,
        "y0": 0.7550523681255006,
        "x1": 0.783032274877367,
        "y1": 0.7656859938362529
      },
      "text": "(4)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.20242634214049382,
        "y0": 0.28649176460780623,
        "x1": 0.876648596521089,
        "y1": 0.32001445072655127
      },
      "text": "where L is deﬁned via the Fourier transform as Lu(ξ) = |ξ|α+1 ω(ξ), with α > 0.",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.15031177097038884,
        "y0": 0.38753913989292627,
        "x1": 0.7796365690062674,
        "y1": 0.3892157973974321
      },
      "text": "Carvajal and Panthee [5] proved that the equation (2) is locally well - posed in Hs(R) for some s depending on α and k. Moreover, if s < max{0, 21 − αk }, the equation (2) is ill - posed in Hs(R), which means that the solution map is not Ck+1 - diﬀerentiable from Hs(R) to C([0, T];Hs(R)) for any T > 0. When α = 1, some global well - posedness results for (2) with periodic boundary conditions were obtained [3].",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.7946684489334798,
        "y0": 0.6418647147289703,
        "x1": 0.8072345191714929,
        "y1": 0.7449402889273059
      },
      "text": "(3)",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "picture",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2887650677643736,
        "y0": 0.7811670891313576,
        "x1": 0.4006714564253106,
        "y1": 0.8499793881477411
      },
      "text": null,
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.14707529133156308,
        "y0": 0.16130748551468638,
        "x1": 0.9208294489776163,
        "y1": 0.18007823481718616
      },
      "text": "Bona and Tzvetkov [1] proved that the BBM equation is globally well - posed in Hs(R) for s ≥ 0. The same result also holds for the periodic case [2, 3]. This well posedness is optimal, since if s < 0, the equation (1) is ill - posed in Hs(R). In fact, Bona and Tzvetkov [1] also proved that for s < 0, the solution map u0  → u(t) of the equation (1) is not a C2 map from Hs(R) to C([0, T]; Hs(R)).",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.2370771902645849,
        "y0": 0.5425589649265053,
        "x1": 0.3455700109845419,
        "y1": 0.5734674359857816
      },
      "text": "α =",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.14785244084857008,
        "y0": 0.5863548042932258,
        "x1": 0.8061179429374833,
        "y1": 0.6108318609262048
      },
      "text": "where A and l represent the wave amplitude and wavelength in the classical sense, h0 represents the undisturbed water depth, and S represents the Stokes number. The ﬁrst - order form of the abcd−system is",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
    {
      "block_type": "text",
      "box": {
        "page": 0,
        "x0": 0.3000132341348254,
        "y0": 0.30220022007706365,
        "x1": 0.6736807945955066,
        "y1": 0.3356100156816378
      },
      "text": "ut + ux + Lut + (uk+1)x = 0, u(0, x) = u0(x),",
      "html": null,
      "level": null,
      "section_hierarchy": []
    },
